<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Reserve Bank of India">
  <data key="d0">Reserve Bank of India</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Reserve Bank of India is the central banking institution of India, which regulates the issue and supply of the Indian rupee and oversees the country's monetary policy.&lt;SEP&gt;The central bank of India, responsible for regulating the issuance and supply of the Indian currency and overseeing the financial system.&lt;SEP&gt;The central banking institution of India, responsible for regulating the issuance and supply of the Indian rupee and overseeing the country's banking system.&lt;SEP&gt;The central banking institution of India, which regulates the country's currency and financial system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Door Step Banking">
  <data key="d0">Door Step Banking</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Door Step Banking refers to a banking service that provides financial services directly at the customer's premises, catering specifically to individuals such as senior citizens and differently-abled persons.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unity Bank">
  <data key="d0">Unity Bank</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Unity Bank is a financial institution that provides various banking services, including doorstep banking to its customers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Senior Citizen">
  <data key="d0">Senior Citizen</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A senior citizen refers to individuals aged over 60 years who are eligible for specific banking services designed to accommodate their needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Differently Abled">
  <data key="d0">Differently Abled</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Differently abled refers to individuals who have physical or mental disabilities that may affect their daily activities, including banking services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KYC Document">
  <data key="d0">KYC Document</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">KYC (Know Your Customer) documents are identification and verification documents that customers must provide to banks to comply with regulatory requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cash Management Vendor">
  <data key="d0">Cash Management Vendor</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A cash management vendor is a company that specializes in the management, transportation, and handling of cash for various financial institutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Charges">
  <data key="d0">Service Charges</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Service charges are fees that banks may levy on customers for providing specific services, which can vary based on the service and customer relationship.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Force Majeure">
  <data key="d0">Force Majeure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Force Majeure refers to unforeseeable circumstances that prevent parties from fulfilling contracts, including natural disasters and other unexpected events.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bank Service Savings Limits">
  <data key="d0">Bank Service Savings Limits</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A table that outlines the savings limits for different types of banking services offered to various customer categories, including service types and monetary limits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cash Pickup">
  <data key="d0">Cash Pickup</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A banking service type that allows customers to withdraw cash from designated locations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cash Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Cash Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A banking service type that allows customers to receive cash delivered to their location.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Savings (Individuals)">
  <data key="d0">Savings (Individuals)</data>
  <data key="d1">customercategory</data>
  <data key="d2">A customer category representing individual account holders with specific savings limits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Senior Citizen / Differently Abled">
  <data key="d0">Senior Citizen / Differently Abled</data>
  <data key="d1">customercategory</data>
  <data key="d2">A customer category that includes senior citizens and differently abled individuals, with tailored savings limits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Current Account Customers">
  <data key="d0">Current Account Customers</data>
  <data key="d1">customercategory</data>
  <data key="d2">A customer category consisting of individuals holding a current account, offering higher savings limits compared to other categories.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bank Policy">
  <data key="d0">Bank Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The guidelines and regulations established by banks, which influence the savings limits and other banking services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="tb-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-0001">
  <data key="d0">tb-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-0001</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">[Table Name]bank_service_savings_limits

This table outlines the savings limits per instance for different types of banking services offered to various customer categories. The rows represent types of services, specifically 'Cash Pickup' and 'Cash Delivery'. The columns delineate the specific savings limits applicable to three distinct customer categories: 'Savings (individuals)', 'Senior Citizen / Differently Abled', and 'Current Account Customers'. Each service allows individuals and senior citizens/differently abled customers to save up to 20,000 per instance, while current account customers have a significantly higher limit of 5 lacs per instance. Notably, the distinction in savings limits highlights the banks' approach to meet different needs across customer segments. The values are presented clearly, with all monetary amounts expressed as per instance, and the note at the bottom indicates that savings limits are subject to change per bank policy. This table serves as a guideline for customers to understand the limits connected to their specific service type and demographic category.

[Table Footnotes]# Subject to change from time to time as per banks policy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786964808</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Banking System">
  <data key="d0">Banking System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An organized system that manages the acceptance of deposits and the lending of funds among various financial institutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Banking Regulation Act, 1949">
  <data key="d0">Banking Regulation Act, 1949</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A legislative framework in India that governs the functioning and operations of banks, enshrining the rights of depositors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unity Small Finance Bank Limited">
  <data key="d0">Unity Small Finance Bank Limited</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A financial institution that offers various deposit products and services to customers, emphasizing the rights and interests of depositors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Depositors">
  <data key="d0">Depositors</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals who place their money into deposit accounts at banks, forming a key stakeholder group in the banking system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deposit Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Deposit Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Accounts held by depositors that allow them to deposit money and earn interest, with specific terms and conditions governing their use.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interest Rates">
  <data key="d0">Interest Rates</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The percentage at which interest is paid by depositors on their deposits held in banks, subject to guidelines from regulatory bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Conditions specifying the rate of interest applicable to various types of deposits, including NRE and NRO deposits.&lt;SEP&gt;Interest rates represent the proportion of a loan or deposit that is charged as interest to the borrower or paid to the depositor, expressed as a percentage of the principal.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bank">
  <data key="d0">Bank</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bank is a financial institution that offers various deposit products, including Demand Deposits and Time Deposits, to customers under different schemes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bank is responsible for providing various banking services, including account management and deposit facilities. It serves as the regulatory body for deposit accounts and offers guidance on account operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bank offers various banking products and services to customers, including debit cards, mobile banking, and access to ATM networks.&lt;SEP&gt;A financial institution that offers banking services, including interest rates on various types of deposit accounts, and operates under specific policies and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The institution that manages term deposits and related financial services.&lt;SEP&gt;The financial institution that provides various banking services, including managing customer accounts, facilitating transactions, and implementing customer service policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Demand Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Demand Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Demand Deposits refer to deposits received by the Bank that can be withdrawn on demand by customers without prior notice.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Time Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time Deposits are deposits received by the Bank for a fixed period and include products like Recurring and Fixed Deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Savings Account">
  <data key="d0">Savings Account</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A Savings Account is a form of Demand Deposit subject to restrictions on the number and amount of withdrawals permitted by the Bank during specified periods.&lt;SEP&gt;An account type that can be opened by an individual, allowing for deposits and withdrawals with interest.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account">
  <data key="d0">Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account (BSBDA) is a type of Savings Account offered as per the guidelines of the Reserve Bank of India (RBI).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Current Account">
  <data key="d0">Current Account</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A Current Account is a type of Demand Deposit that allows withdrawals any number of times up to a specific agreed amount.&lt;SEP&gt;An account type designed for frequent transactions and is typically used by businesses for managing cash flows.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cash Credit">
  <data key="d0">Cash Credit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cash Credit is a credit facility provided by banks to borrowers, which allows them to withdraw money as needed within a limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Overdraft">
  <data key="d0">Overdraft</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Overdraft is a banking service that allows customers to withdraw more money than they have in their accounts, up to a certain limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RBI">
  <data key="d0">RBI</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) is the central banking institution of India, overseeing monetary policy and regulation of banks.&lt;SEP&gt;Reserve Bank of India, the central banking institution in India that regulates monetary policy.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) is the central banking institution of India responsible for regulating the country's monetary policy and managing its currency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Know Your Customer">
  <data key="d0">Know Your Customer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Know Your Customer (KYC) is a process used by banks to verify the identity of their clients to prevent fraud.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Permanent Account Number">
  <data key="d0">Permanent Account Number</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Permanent Account Number (PAN) is a unique identifier issued by the Indian Income Tax Department to track financial transactions and tax compliance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recurring Deposit">
  <data key="d0">Recurring Deposit</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A Recurring Deposit is a form of Time Deposit where the customer contributes a fixed amount at regular intervals instead of a lump sum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Short Term Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Short Term Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Short Term Deposits are a category of Time Deposits that are accepted for a shorter duration compared to standard fixed deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Limited Liability Partnership">
  <data key="d0">Limited Liability Partnership</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Limited Liability Partnership is a business structure that combines elements of partnerships and corporations, providing limited liability to its owners.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customers">
  <data key="d0">Customers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Customers refer to individuals or entities that avail banking services, including the opening and maintenance of various deposit accounts.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals or entities that maintain accounts and utilize the services provided by the bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Specified Associates">
  <data key="d0">Specified Associates</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Specified Associates are defined groups or organizations that are allowed to open accounts with the Bank under certain conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Debit Card">
  <data key="d0">Debit Card</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A payment card issued by the Bank to customers having Saving Bank or Current Accounts, enabling them to perform transactions according to regulatory guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mobile Banking">
  <data key="d0">Mobile Banking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A service provided by the Bank that allows customers to perform banking transactions through mobile devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="WhatsApp Banking">
  <data key="d0">WhatsApp Banking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A service offered by the Bank enabling customers to conduct banking transactions via WhatsApp.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internet Banking">
  <data key="d0">Internet Banking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An online banking service provided by the Bank for customers to manage their accounts and transactions over the internet.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ATM Network">
  <data key="d0">ATM Network</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Network enabling customers to access ATMs belonging to the Bank as well as other banks, regulated by authorities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NEFT">
  <data key="d0">NEFT</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">National Electronic Funds Transfer, a service provided by the Bank for the electronic transfer of funds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RTGS">
  <data key="d0">RTGS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Real Time Gross Settlement, another electronic funds transfer method offered by the Bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statement of Account">
  <data key="d0">Statement of Account</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A summary report provided to customers on their account activity, available in digital form and accessible via various banking platforms.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minor Account">
  <data key="d0">Minor Account</data>
  <data key="d1">account</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of account that can be opened for a minor, operated by a guardian or the minor themselves if above a certain age.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Account">
  <data key="d0">Joint Account</data>
  <data key="d1">account</data>
  <data key="d2">An account held by two or more individuals that can be operated under various mandates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power of Attorney">
  <data key="d0">Power of Attorney</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A legal document that allows a designated person to operate a Bank account on behalf of the account holder.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nomination">
  <data key="d0">Nomination</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A facility allowing account holders to designate individuals who will inherit account balances upon their demise.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nominee">
  <data key="d0">Nominee</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Nominee is a person, who receives the outstanding balance in a deposit account in the event of the depositor's death, serving as a trustee for the legal heirs.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual designated to receive the proceeds of a term deposit upon the death of the depositor.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual designated to receive the balance from a bank account in the event of the account holder's demise.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Depositor">
  <data key="d0">Depositor</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Depositor is an individual who opens and manages a deposit account with the bank and may nominate another person to receive funds upon the depositor's death.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual who places money in a bank's term deposit account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Senior Citizens">
  <data key="d0">Senior Citizens</data>
  <data key="d1">population</data>
  <data key="d2">Senior Citizens refers to Resident Indian individuals aged over 60 years who may be eligible for higher interest rates on fixed deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Illiterate Person">
  <data key="d0">Illiterate Person</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An Illiterate Person is an individual who may open a deposit account under conditions set by the bank, requiring personal attendance and a witness.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visually Challenged Persons">
  <data key="d0">Visually Challenged Persons</data>
  <data key="d1">population</data>
  <data key="d2">Visually Challenged Persons are individuals who may open deposit accounts which they operate personally, with assistance from bank officials if necessary.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Persons with Disabilities">
  <data key="d0">Persons with Disabilities</data>
  <data key="d1">population</data>
  <data key="d2">Persons with Disabilities refers to individuals covered under the National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and Multiple Disabilities Act, 1999, who can have accounts managed by guardians.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian">
  <data key="d0">Guardian</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Guardian is a person appointed to manage the care and property of individuals with disabilities or minors, often required to facilitate banking transactions on their behalf.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transgender Person">
  <data key="d0">Transgender Person</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A Transgender Person is recognized as 'Third Gender' in banking operations, and they should be treated equally as other customers without discrimination.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer">
  <data key="d0">Customer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Customer is any individual using the banking services provided by the bank, including account openings, withdrawals, and closures.&lt;SEP&gt;A customer is an individual or entity that has taken out a loan or has a deposit account with a bank and engages with the financial services provided.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Domestic, Non-Resident Ordinary Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Domestic, Non-Resident Ordinary Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Types of bank accounts designated for non-resident individuals to manage their income earned in India, offering specific interest rate conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Resident (External) Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Non-Resident (External) Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Types of accounts meant for non-resident Indians to hold foreign currency and manage funds internationally, with guidelines for interest payments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Domestic Current Account">
  <data key="d0">Domestic Current Account</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of bank account that typically does not earn interest but allows for frequent transactions and is designed for businesses or individuals needing liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Domestic Savings Bank Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Domestic Savings Bank Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Bank accounts that earn interest on deposits and offer flexibility for withdrawals and deposits, with interest calculated on a daily product basis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Domestic Term Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Domestic Term Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Deposits made with a set term, with fixed interest rates determined by the bank and governed by Reserve Bank of India guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Term Deposit">
  <data key="d0">Term Deposit</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A financial product where a depositor invests money for a fixed period at a specified interest rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Legal Heirs">
  <data key="d0">Legal Heirs</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals who are entitled by law to inherit the assets of a deceased person.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tax Deduction Certificate">
  <data key="d0">Tax Deduction Certificate</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A document issued by the bank certifying the amount of tax deducted at source on interest earned.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Form 15G">
  <data key="d0">Form 15G</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A form used by depositors to declare that their total income is below the taxable limit to avoid TDS.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Form 15H">
  <data key="d0">Form 15H</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A form similar to Form 15G, but specifically for senior citizens to claim exemption from TDS.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Master Policy on Customer Service">
  <data key="d0">Master Policy on Customer Service</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A document detailing the policies and guidelines related to customer service and term deposits.&lt;SEP&gt;A comprehensive policy document outlining the bank's customer service procedures, rights, and obligations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NRE/NRO Deposit Scheme">
  <data key="d0">NRE/NRO Deposit Scheme</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A scheme allowing non-resident Indians to deposit money under specific terms and conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Premature Withdrawal Penalty">
  <data key="d0">Premature Withdrawal Penalty</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A financial penalty applied by banks for withdrawing a term deposit before its maturity date.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NRE Deposit">
  <data key="d0">NRE Deposit</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">NRE deposits refer to Non-Resident External deposits that are maintained by non-resident Indians in banks in India, specifically catered to foreign currency earnings.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NRO Deposit">
  <data key="d0">NRO Deposit</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">NRO deposits refer to Non-Resident Ordinary deposits that are maintained by non-resident Indians for managing income earned in India.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scheduled Commercial Banks">
  <data key="d0">Scheduled Commercial Banks</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Scheduled Commercial Banks are banks in India that are included in the Second Schedule of the Reserve Bank of India Act, 1934, and are engaged in providing banking services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deposit Insurance and Credit Guarantee Corporation of India (DICGC)">
  <data key="d0">Deposit Insurance and Credit Guarantee Corporation of India (DICGC)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">DICGC is a government corporation in India that provides insurance for deposits held by consumers in banks, offering protection against bank failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Board of Directors">
  <data key="d0">Board of Directors</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Board of Directors is a group of individuals elected to represent shareholders and oversee the activities and policy-making of an organization, such as a bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Information">
  <data key="d0">Customer Information</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer information refers to the data collected from customers by banks, which can be used for various purposes, including cross-selling services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KYC Documents">
  <data key="d0">KYC Documents</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">KYC (Know Your Customer) documents are necessary identification documents that banks require to verify the identity of their customers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inactive Account">
  <data key="d0">Inactive Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An inactive account is a bank account that has not had any customer-initiated transactions for a specified period, leading to its classification for monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dormant Account">
  <data key="d0">Dormant Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A dormant account is a bank account which has been inactive for an extended period, typically two years, prompting banks to classify it as dormant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unclaimed Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Unclaimed Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unclaimed deposits are funds in bank accounts that have not been accessed by the account holder for a designated period, usually resulting in their transfer to a regulatory authority.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insurance Cover for Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Insurance Cover for Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insurance cover for deposits refers to the financial protection provided to bank depositors by the DICGC, safeguarding their deposits up to a certain limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786967977</data>
